<FONT SIZE=+3>Ontonagon (6210)</FONT>

<P>&nbsp;The following tables are the 1951-1980 Normals and Narrative Summary

<P>1. <A HREF="http://climate.geo.msu.edu/Stations/6210/TMP1_NM.TXT">Temperature
normals and extremes</A>

<P>2. <A HREF="http://climate.geo.msu.edu/Stations/6210/TMP2_NM.TXT">Heating &amp;
cooling degree days, and number of days for selected thresholds</A>

<P>3. <A HREF="http://climate.geo.msu.edu/Stations/6210/prec_nm.txt">Precipitation
normals</A>

<P>4. <A HREF="http://climate.geo.msu.edu/Stations/6210/narrat.txt">Narrative summary</A>

<P>The following tables are statistical probabilities based on the 1951-1980
data

<P>using the indicated Probability Distribution Function (PDF).

<P>5. <A HREF="http://climate.geo.msu.edu/Stations/6210/tmax_st.txt">Average daily
maximum temperature (Normal PDF)</A>

<P>6. <A HREF="http://climate.geo.msu.edu/Stations/6210/tmin_st.txt">Average daily
minimum temperature (Normal PDF)</A>

<P>7. <A HREF="http://climate.geo.msu.edu/Stations/6210/tmen_st.txt">Average daily
mean temperature (Normal PDF)</A>

<P>8. <A HREF="http://climate.geo.msu.edu/Stations/6210/hdd65_st.txt">Monthly &amp;
seasonal (July-June) heating degree-days base 65 F (Gamma PDF)</A>

<P>9. <A HREF="http://climate.geo.msu.edu/Stations/6210/cdd65_st.txt">Monthly &amp;
annual cooling degree days-base 65 F (Gamma PDF)</A>

<P>10. <A HREF="http://climate.geo.msu.edu/Stations/6210/txg90_st.txt">Number of
days with maximum Temperature of 90 F or above (Weibull PDF)</A>

<P>11. <A HREF="http://climate.geo.msu.edu/Stations/6210/txl32_st.txt">Number of
days with maximum Temperature of 32 F or below (Weibull PDF)</A>

<P>12. <A HREF="http://climate.geo.msu.edu/Stations/6210/tnl32_st.txt">Number of
days with minimum Temperature of 32 F or below (Weibull PDF)</A>

<P>13. <A HREF="http://climate.geo.msu.edu/Stations/6210/tnl0_st.txt">Number of
days with minimum Temperature of 0 F or below (Weibull PDF)</A>

<P>14. <A HREF="http://climate.geo.msu.edu/Stations/6210/l_spr_st.txt">Last spring
temperature threshold date (Normal PDF)</A>

<P>15. <A HREF="http://climate.geo.msu.edu/Stations/6210/f_fal_st.txt">First fall
temperature threshold date (Normal PDF)</A>

<P>16. <A HREF="http://climate.geo.msu.edu/Stations/6210/g_sea_st.txt">Growing
season length between threshold dates (Normal PDF)</A>

<P>17. <A HREF="http://climate.geo.msu.edu/Stations/6210/gdd40_st.txt">Monthly
&amp; seasonal (Mar-Oct) growing degree-days base 40 F (Gamma PDF)</A>

<P>18. <A HREF="http://climate.geo.msu.edu/Stations/6210/gdd45_st.txt">Monthly
&amp; seasonal (Mar-Oct) growing degree-days base 45 F (Gamma PDF)</A>

<P>19. <A HREF="http://climate.geo.msu.edu/Stations/6210/gdd50_st.txt">Monthly
&amp; seasonal (Mar-Oct) growing degree-days base 50 F (Gamma PDF)</A>

<P>20. <A HREF="http://climate.geo.msu.edu/Stations/6210/gdd55_st.txt">Monthly
&amp; seasonal (Mar-Oct) growing degree-days base 55 F (Gamma PDF)</A>

<P>21. <A HREF="http://climate.geo.msu.edu/Stations/6210/g8650_st.txt">Monthly
&amp; seasonal (Mar-Oct) growing degree-days, corn method (86max &amp;
50min) (Gamma PDF)</A>

<P>22. <A HREF="http://climate.geo.msu.edu/Stations/6210/prec_st.txt">Monthly &amp;
annual total precipitation (Gamma PDF)</A>

<P>23. <A HREF="http://climate.geo.msu.edu/Stations/6210/snow_st.txt">Monthly &amp;
seasonal (Sep-May) total snowfall (Gamma PDF)</A>

<P>24. <A HREF="http://climate.geo.msu.edu/Stations/6210/dpg10_st.txt"># of days
with precipitation of .10 inch or above (Weibull PDF)</A>

<P>25. <A HREF="http://climate.geo.msu.edu/Stations/6210/dpg25_st.txt"># of days
with precipitation of .25 inch or above (Weibull PDF)</A>

<P>26. <A HREF="http://climate.geo.msu.edu/Stations/6210/dpg50_st.txt"># of days
with precipitation of .50 inch or above (Weibull PDF)</A>

<P>27. <A HREF="http://climate.geo.msu.edu/Stations/6210/prssn_st.txt">Monthly
&amp; seasonal (Apr-Sep) precipitation (Gamma PDF)</A>

